{
  "version": 1,
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "c_t30001",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# TypeScript across cells",
        "",
        "Write TypeScript in every cell and let the editor follow your types from one cell to the next.",
        "",
        "You will hover a name to read its type, complete a property, read a type error in the Problems panel and rename a name in every cell at once. About 7 minutes.",
        "",
        "Every code cell is TypeScript (plain JavaScript is TypeScript too). The editor checks the whole notebook as one program: a type a cell declares is known to the cells below it. Click **Run All** first."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t30002",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 1. A type, then values of that type"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t30003",
      "type": "server",
      "source": [
        "type Plant = {",
        "  name: string;",
        "  waterEveryDays: number;",
        "  lastWatered: Date;",
        "};",
        "",
        "const plants: Plant[] = [",
        "  { name: \"fern\", waterEveryDays: 3, lastWatered: new Date(\"2026-03-01\") },",
        "  { name: \"cactus\", waterEveryDays: 21, lastWatered: new Date(\"2026-02-10\") },",
        "  { name: \"basil\", waterEveryDays: 1, lastWatered: new Date(\"2026-03-03\") },",
        "];"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t30004",
      "type": "server",
      "source": [
        "function nextWatering(plant: Plant): Date {",
        "  const next = new Date(plant.lastWatered);",
        "  next.setDate(next.getDate() + plant.waterEveryDays);",
        "  return next;",
        "}",
        "",
        "plants.map((plant) => ({ name: plant.name, next: nextWatering(plant).toDateString() }))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t30005",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 2. Hover and complete",
        "",
        "- Hover `plants` or `nextWatering` in the cell above: a box shows its type, though both were declared in other cells. Right after the notebook opens, the first hover can take a few seconds while the language service starts.",
        "- In the cell below, delete `name` after `plants[0].` and press **Ctrl+Space**: the list offers `lastWatered`, `name` and `waterEveryDays`, with the type of the one selected beside it. Pick `waterEveryDays` with **Enter** and run the cell."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t30006",
      "type": "server",
      "source": [
        "plants[0].name"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t30007",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "While you type a call such as `nextWatering(`, a box under the cursor shows the function's parameters. **F12** (or Cmd+click) on a name goes to where it is declared, even in another cell."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t30008",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 3. Type errors",
        "",
        "The next cell passes a plant without `lastWatered`, so TypeScript underlines `mint` in `nextWatering(mint)` in red. Hover the red line to read the error.",
        "",
        "The status bar at the bottom counts the errors and warnings; click it, or press **Cmd+Shift+M**, to open **Problems**, the list of every error in the notebook. Click an entry to go to its line."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t30009",
      "type": "server",
      "source": [
        "const mint = { name: \"mint\", waterEveryDays: 2 };",
        "nextWatering(mint)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t30010",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Types are checked, not enforced: the cell still runs. Here it does not even fail: it answers `Invalid Date`, exactly the mistake the red line warned about. Add `lastWatered: new Date()` to `mint` and the error goes away.",
        "",
        "From a terminal, `nimbo check -n tutorial/03-typescript.jsnb` prints the same errors without running anything."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t30011",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 4. Rename everywhere",
        "",
        "Click on `nextWatering` in any cell and press **F2**. Type `nextWateringDate` and press **Enter**: the declaration and every use, in every cell, change together.",
        "",
        "F2 renames a name in the code. On a selected cell (after **Escape**), F2 renames the cell itself, as in the first lesson."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c_t30012",
      "type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Try it",
        "",
        "1. Add `room: \"kitchen\" | \"bedroom\"` to the `Plant` type. Which cells get red lines? Fix them.",
        "2. Write `plants.filter((plant) => plant.` in a new cell and use completion to finish it.",
        "",
        "Next: `04-client-and-bridge`, cells that run in the page and call the server."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
